00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.751
after midnight.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.251
Look at this.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.052
It's an early morning

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:19.953
truth social post

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.920
from the former president

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.654
insisting

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.223
any charge in the hush money case

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.258
could unleash, quote, death

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.459
and destruction.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.227
With me in studio

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:27.994
to share their reporting

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:30.330
and their insights CNN's Lauren Fox.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.298
Dylan Young of The New York Times.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.334
And NPR's Tamara Keith.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.935
Death could unleash death

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.003
and destruction.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.105
Catastrophic for our country.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.243
He should know better.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.512
This it's now been two,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.046
three years

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.447
where we've had

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.883
law enforcement agencies across the gamut

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.084
have been warning

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.952
about the risk of political violence

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.687
and how some of the claims

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.555
from public officials,

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.690
false claims continued to motivate

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.259
some of that political violence

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.628
and make that threat more severe.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:03.963
We saw similar chatter ahead of January

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.598
six online as well.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:06.399
This is blatant

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.968
forecasting of potential violence here.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.203
And we've learned

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.204
through the past couple of years

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:11.504
that there's

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.640
consequences to this as well.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.841
Let me just interrupt at that point

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:15.942
just to bring into the conversation.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:16.676
Look, Donald Trump's

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.911
not gonna listen to Hakeem Jeffries.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:18.812
He's the top Democrat

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:19.879
in the House of Representatives.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.981
Now, but you will get a chance to listen

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.417
to Hakeem Jeffries here. And guess what?

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.952
Most Republicans will say this publicly.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:26.786
Privately, they'll tell you

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:27.487
they agree with just

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:28.588
about every word of this

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.990
Well, the twice impeached

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.227
former president's rhetoric is reckless,

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.996
reprehensible and irresponsible.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.666
It's dangerous

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.000
and if he keeps it up,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.670
he's going to get someone killed.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.307
We've already seen the consequences

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.144
of incitement from the former president.

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.379
And the former president

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.314
